                        "form": "testers"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "60730b29-5755-3d7c-ad54-b836b525b323",
                        "entry_id": "47c7c016-2e18-380b-a007-45b24bc31a1a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative form of testiere (“armor for a horse's head”)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "alternative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ebb8f8f-7983-43cc-b935-8a28c9d3986e",
                                "sense_id": "60730b29-5755-3d7c-ad54-b836b525b323",
                                "text": "A horse-head tester had cutouts for the animal's eyes and ears. A peytral protected the horse's breast, while the crinet, made of overlapping steel plates joined by leather straps or rivets, protected its neck."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f260a0a3-57c0-4235-b37e-74ddb305b0bd",
                                "sense_id": "60730b29-5755-3d7c-ad54-b836b525b323",
                                "text": "The tester and crupper, together with the piser, which probably protected the chest, formed the basis of most horse armour[…]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
